From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, kernelbase, netapi32, crypt32, dxgi: small stubs that answered wrongly, second set

- NtQueryInformationFile: FileStatLxInformation (FileStatInformation and
  the Linux side of the file: owner, group, mode, device numbers),
  FileCaseSensitiveInformation (no directory is case sensitive: names
  match without case, as on Windows by default) and
  FileStorageReserveIdInformation (StorageReserveIdNone) returned
  STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED ("Unsupported info class").
- GetLongPathNameW gave a \\?\ or UNC path back as it was ("UNC
  pathname" fixme): now the part naming no file (\\server\share, \\?\C:,
  \\?\UNC\server\share, \\?\Volume{...}) is kept, the rest is expanded
  and must exist (ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND otherwise); \\.\ device paths come
  back as they are. The path is no longer limited to 1024 characters.
- NetGetJoinInformation said "Workgroup": a computer that is not a domain
  member is in Samba's workgroup (smb.conf [global] workgroup) or in
  WORKGROUP, as on Windows. SG_SMB_CONF names a stand-in for gates.
- CertControlStore(CERT_STORE_CTRL_NOTIFY_CHANGE) did nothing: the event
  is signalled when the store's registry key (or one under it) changes;
  CERT_STORE_CTRL_RESYNC with an event arms it again.
- NtSetInformationVirtualMemory(VmPrefetchInformation) reads this
  process's pages ahead quietly; only another process's is reported.
- dxgi: the back buffer, shared, read-only and discard-on-present usages
  describe a buffer and are not bind flags ("Unhandled DXGI usage 0x40").

Wine's kernel32 path tests: one todo_wine passes and is removed; ntdll
file, crypt32 store and netapi32 wksta tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/smallstubs2-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_LX_INFO (ntdll/unix/file.c), SG_MUTANT_UNC_AS_IS
(kernelbase/file.c), SG_MUTANT_FIXED_WORKGROUP (netapi32/netapi32.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_STORE_NOTIFY (crypt32/regstore.c).
